#question(title: [Proving something is an indeterminate form])[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  + Prove that $display(forall c in RR)$,
    $display(exists a in RR)$ and functions
    $f$ and $g$ such that
     $
       lim_(x -> a) f(x) = 0, quad lim_(x -> a) g(x) = 0, quad lim_(x -> a) (f(x))/(g(x)) = c
     $

     This is how you show that $display(0/0)$
     is an indeterminate form.
  + Prove the same way that $display(oo/oo)$,
    $display(0 dot.op oo)$, and
    $display(oo - oo)$ are also indeterminate
    forms.
  + Prove that $display(1^oo)$,
    $display(0^0)$, and $display(oo^0)$ are
    indeterminate forms.

     (You will only get $c >= 0$ this time)
]
